<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<AssetDeclaration xmlns="uri:ea.com:eala:asset">

    <!-- ==================================================================
         Chaos Drone gas — "dissident" (insane) effect  [WORKING]
         ==================================================================
         KW's Redeemer "Rage Generator" is the closest shipped precedent for
         the Chaos Drone, and it is implemented with XML only:

             KW GlobalData/Weapon.xml ~12812-12836
                 <WeaponTemplate id="NODWarmechRageGenerator"
                                 RadiusDamageAffects="ENEMIES NEUTRALS">
                   <Nuggets>
                     <DamageNugget Damage="0" Radius="500.0" .../>
                     <AttributeModifierNugget
                         AttributeModifierName="AttributeModifier_Hallucinate"
                         Radius="500">
                       <SpecialObjectFilter Rule="ANY"
                           Include="INFANTRY VEHICLE" Exclude="AIRCRAFT"/>
                     </AttributeModifierNugget>
                   </Nuggets>
                 </WeaponTemplate>

             KW GlobalData/AttributeModifier.xml:146-151
                 <AttributeModifier id="AttributeModifier_Hallucinate"
                     Category="NONE" Duration="6s"
                     ModelConditionsSet="EMOTION_DISSIDENT"/>

         i.e. the ONLY effect applied to the victim is the model condition
         EMOTION_DISSIDENT; the hostility flip, the loss of player control and
         the auto-recovery are all engine-side. That is the real meaning of
         "EMOTION_DISSIDENT is defected in nature" (see dev-notes.md).

         RA3 still ships every part of that code path:
             EMOTION_DISSIDENT      Schemas/Includes/ModelState.xsd:425
             ObjectDefectionHelper  Xml/BaseObjects/BaseObject.xml:31-35
                                    (present on EVERY RA3 object)
             TEMPORARILY_DEFECTED   Schemas/Includes/ObjectStatus.xsd:71
             TemporarilyDefectUpdate Schemas/Modules/TemporarilyDefectUpdate.xsd:8

         RESULT IN RA3 (verified in game 2026-10-24): it WORKS. Units hit by the
         gas turn on their own teammates and revert by themselves when the
         Duration expires.

         The ONE thing the engine does NOT do is re-evaluate an attack order that
         was already issued: a unit that was shooting the CD owner before the gas
         keeps shooting it. That gap is closed in Lua — BecomeDissidentFunction
         in Scripts.lua, triggered by the LuaEventNugget in WeaponTemplate.xml.
         (In YR an insane unit never keeps pounding the Chaos Drone, so that step
         is required for parity.)
         ================================================================== -->

    <!-- ACTIVE. The one and only effect needed — verified working in game.

         NON_AUTOACQUIRABLE + HYBRID.

         Goal (YR behaviour): the insane unit attacks everybody, but its own
         former allies leave it alone, while the player can still order attacks
         on it.

         Statuses are per OBJECT and apply to every observer, so:
           - UNATTACKABLE       -> nobody can hit it, including the player (rejected)
           - no status at all   -> insane units fight each other, but their own
                                   former allies shoot them dead (observed)
         NON_AUTOACQUIRABLE is the right half-measure, but it also hides the victim
         from OTHER insane units (observed: insane units stopped fighting each
         other).

         So the other half is done in Lua: BecomeDissidentFunction keeps a roster
         of currently insane units and issues explicit UNIT_CONTEXT_SENSITIVE_ATTACK
         orders between them. Explicit orders bypass the auto-acquire filter, so
         insane units still turn on each other while normal units leave them be. -->
    <AttributeModifier
        id="AttributeModifier_Dissident"
        Category="NONE"
        Duration="20s"
        ModelConditionsSet="EMOTION_DISSIDENT"
        ObjectStatusToSet="NON_AUTOACQUIRABLE" />

    <!-- REMOVED: AttributeModifier_NoAttackPulse (NO_ATTACK for 0.5s).
         Tested 2026-10-24: NO_ATTACK only suppresses firing, it does NOT cancel
         the attack order, so victims still kept shooting the drone — the only
         visible effect was a 0.5s stutter on every gas tick.
         Clearing the order really does need Lua (NAMED_STOP), which in turn
         needs a LUAEventList on every unit — see UnitOverrides/UnitOverrides.xml.
    -->

    <!-- Alternative, NOT in use: the same thing plus TEMPORARILY_DEFECTED.
         Prepared as a fallback while we still believed the model condition did
         nothing. Unnecessary now that EMOTION_DISSIDENT is confirmed to work;
         kept in case we ever want the engine's own defection bookkeeping
         (TemporarilyDefectUpdate) involved. Status names are strings on purpose
         — the numeric ObjectStatusTable in Scripts.lua has drifted. -->
    <AttributeModifier
        id="AttributeModifier_DissidentStatus"
        Category="NONE"
        Duration="20s"
        ModelConditionsSet="EMOTION_DISSIDENT"
        ObjectStatusToSet="TEMPORARILY_DEFECTED" />

    <!-- Legacy Lua-driven implementation. Kept as a fallback for the Phase 2b
         route: it only tags the victim as un-auto-acquirable, the actual
         defection is done in BecomeDissidentFunction(). -->
    <AttributeModifier
        id="AttributeModifier_Hallucinate"
        Category="NONE"
        Duration="20s"
        ObjectStatusToSet="NON_AUTOACQUIRABLE" >
    </AttributeModifier>

    <AttributeModifier
        id="AttributeModifer_ChaosGenerator"
        ObjectStatusToSet="GENERIC_TOGGLE_STATE" >
        <Modifier Type="SPEED" Value="0%"/>
    </AttributeModifier>

    <AttributeModifier
        id="AttributeModifer_ChaosGeneratorTrigger"
        ObjectStatusToSet="GENERIC_TOGGLE_STATE" >
    </AttributeModifier>
</AssetDeclaration>
